[test-suite name=live ring=2
  [doc [#
conformance fixtures for cx-stdlib/live (pack spec spec/02-working/live.md;
ruled design spec/_archived/live_modes.md L129–L137 + the §10 U1 binding —
campaign stream 3, #675). W1 corpus: the stateless core `changes-since`;
W2 corpus (cases 020+): the live ∂ subscription `observe` and its
delivery.md §4 consumption arms ([?receive] / [?select] / [?close]).

   Each program imports the bundled modules ([?lib 'cx-stdlib/store'] /
   'cx-stdlib/journal' / 'cx-stdlib/live'), builds a hermetic mem:// source,
   and calls [$live:changes-since Q BIND CURSOR]. Executing the quoted
   comprehension requires the `eval` capability (the L99 sandbox posture),
   so behavior cases carry grant='eval read write' and the deny lane pins
   CXER0271. Every case uses its OWN mem:// URL (mem stores of one
   canonical root are shared process-wide, #628).

   THE W1 FIXTURE FAMILIES (ledger done-when + live_modes §8):

   (1) EQUIVALENCE-QUARTET LEG 1 — a one-time [?for] ≡ changes-since from
   the EMPTY cursor [head-set]: the exact ∂ is the full relation as
   inserts, for EVERY comprehension (incl. τ members, live-010 — the
   universal empty-cursor exception; no [recompute] marker).

   (2) HEAD-SET ROUND-TRIP — the returned cursor fed back verbatim answers
   the empty ∂ at quiescence, exactly the new inserts after source
   advance, and [retract pos=] after a delete. Consumers re-wrap the
   cursor entries ([?element "head-set" $c/head-set]) because a path
   binding unwraps a single matched element to its content.

   (3) ∂ / RECOMPUTE SHAPE PARITY (L131 transparency) — the ROW inside a ∂
   frame is byte-equal to the recompute relation's row at the same
   position ($cx:equal-pinned), for σ/π and for γ ([regroup] carries the
   full group row; a γ retract answers the honest [recompute reason=…] +
   full-relation-as-inserts form, reason text = the planar_delta marker
   verbatim).

   Plus the pack's typed refusals as first implemented: CXER5070
   not-a-quoted-planar-comprehension, CXER0120 membership (reused),
   CXER5071 unbound/mis-kinded formal, CXER5072 invalid cursor, CXER5073
   resume below retention (post-prune history loss), CXER0271 eval-cap
   deny. Journal sources exercise the per-stream seq cursor (the one
   deliberate L99 widening: store AND journal sources under $bind).

   THE W2 FIXTURE FAMILIES (ledger done-when + live_modes §8):

   (4) EQUIVALENCE-QUARTET LEG 2 — observe ≡ repeated changes-since
   driven by source advance: each [?receive] answers the LITERAL
   changes-since value from the subscription's cursor (021 pins three
   rounds byte-equal, incl. a retract round and a quiescent round).

   (5) ∂-NEVER-COALESCES — the burst discriminator: N inserts ⇒ N
   [insert] frames, never merged (022); retention=latest on a ∂ stream
   is the structural CXER5075 policy refusal (025).

   (6) THE HANDLE IS A delivery.md §4 SUBSCRIPTION — rung= always
   reported (:complete-ordered for native sources; weakest-of-set for a
   mixed store+journal set), sharing/flow/retention declared, the client
   anchor as the [head-set] child, on-close + [?with-open] composition,
   [?close] via the shared close contract (023/024/029/030).

   (7) RESUME + TERMINATION — observe from a pruned-below cursor refuses
   CXER5073 at creation, never a silent re-seed (036); a mid-stream
   fault is delivered LOUD as the FINAL FRAME of a terminal batch whose
   head-set is the unadvanced cursor (031); after it — and after
   [?close] — receive refuses CXER5074 closed-and-drained (028/032).

   (8) QUIESCENCE EXACTNESS — cursor = head on every source ⇒ the exact
   ∂ is EMPTY by identity, for EVERY comprehension incl. τ members
   (037 observe / 038 changes-since — the second universal exactness
   point beside the empty cursor, live.md §3).

   Consumption arms: [?receive from=] unbatched (the next batch),
   [?receive from= max= deadline=] the U1.12a batch form (the sequence
   of non-empty batches, 035), [?select] readiness + timeout fallback
   (033), journal-source subscriptions (034), the $opts guarantee
   declaration (:monotonic-reads/:gapless accepted 027; an
   out-of-vocabulary token refuses CXER5075, 026), observe eval-cap
   deny CXER0271 (039).

   THE W3 FIXTURE FAMILIES (ledger done-when + live_modes §8):

   (9) EQUIVALENCE-QUARTET LEGS 3+4 — materialize ≡ observe + a durable
   fold + an address (043: the read snapshot's rows and head-set equal
   the observe subscription's delivered state at the same coordinate);
   maintained ≡ recompute (044: after a retract window the read equals
   the fresh recompute, $cx:equal-pinned).

   (10) PER-AGGREGATE MAINTENANCE (L130) — sum/count/avg absorb a
   γ-retract (044: `sum` decrements exactly, recomputed=false);
   max/min/distinct force the LOUD group recompute (045:
   recomputed=true, value still exact); maintenance="incremental"
   refuses CXER5076 at creation outside the sub-fragment (046) and at
   any advance whose window forces the recompute (047).

   (11) THE CHECKPOINT IS THE DURABLE CURSOR — [checkpoint q= [head-set]
   ROW…], put-doc-then-alias, expect-pos CAS; derived-state posture: a
   deleted/unreadable checkpoint means FULL REPLAY, same result (048);
   an alias held by a different value refuses CXER1114, never a silent
   replace (049); materialize on its own checkpoint RE-ATTACHES (052).

   (12) RETENTION COVER EXTENDED (L133) — journal-retain refuses while
   a materialization is registered on the stream (051 — the SAME
   snapshot+policy succeeds before registration, refuses after: the
   discriminating pair); journal-source folds advance on the
   per-stream seq, quiescent advance is applied=0 recomputed=false
   (050).

   THE W5 FIXTURE FAMILIES (the §8 sweep + M5):

   (13) THE γ RETRACT/REINSERT GROUP-POSITION PAIR (L94/L131) — a group
   whose member is retracted and a new member reinserted keeps its
   first-appearance position while any member remains (065, maintained
   ≡ recompute pinned); the ∂-never-coalesces vs materialize-read
   COALESCE CONTRAST (066: the same burst is N frames on the ∂ stream
   and ONE point-in-time snapshot on the read).

   (14) M5 END-TO-END (live_modes §8's substrate) — ONE commerce model,
   all four modes composed (067): revenue-by-region as a one-time
   query; changes-since carrying a dashboard cursor (a [regroup] frame
   lands); materialize maintained through a γ-retract window
   (recomputed=false — the retract-incremental leg; the loud boundary
   is 045/047) with maintained ≡ recompute pinned and a quiescent
   advance; an agent observing the :snapshot-diff adapter stream fed
   by the CDC-less order DB through adapt-poll.

   NAMED-WIRE-REF STORES (the W5 store-feed residual): refs are
   wire-created (store_ref_advance_local is the CSRP/XSP listeners'
   funnel), unreachable from public local surface — the per-ref cursor
   ([s source= ref= pos=] streams; exact retract+insert on a ref
   advance; the W1 CXER1709 refusal LIFTED) is pinned by the in-module
   V test vcx/platform/live_refs_feed_test.v.

   Deferred by ruling, none — the pack's ruled families are complete
   at W5; the wire feed over remote stores is stream 4's (L136,
   discharged in the XSP store profile).

   NOTE: no inter-fixture comment blocks appear between cases (a comment
   between sections risks capture into the preceding section payload).
#]]

 [case id=live-001-empty-cursor-full-inserts level=core grant='eval read write'
  [tags live changes-since empty-cursor quartet-leg1 l129 stream-3]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/store']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/live']
[?let [= $s [$store:open "mem://live-doc"]]
[= $h [$store:put-doc $s [order [region "west"] [amount 100]]]]
  [$live:changes-since [?quote [?for [in $o [$store:source $orders "//order"]] [yield $o]]] {orders: $s} [head-set]]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
[changes [head-set [s source=orders pos=1]] [insert pos=0 [order [region 'west'] [amount 100]]]]
#]]
 ]

 [case id=live-002-quartet-leg1-for-equivalence level=core grant='eval read write'
  [tags live changes-since quartet-leg1 equivalence stream-3]
  [in-cx [#
[empty]
#]]
  [in-code [#
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/store']
[?lib 'cx-stdlib/live']
[?let [= $s [$store:open "mem://live-002"]]
[= $h1 [$store:put-doc $s [order id=1 region=east]]]
[= $h2 [$store:put-doc $s [order id=2 region=west]]]
[= $q [?quote [?for [in $o [$store:source $orders "//order"]] [yield $o]]]]
[= $for-rows [?for [in $o [$store:source $s "//order"]] [yield $o]]]
[= $c [$live:changes-since $q {orders: $s} [head-set]]]
[= $cs-rows [?for [in $f $c/insert] [yield [$first $f/*]]]]
  [leg1 eq=[$cx:equal $for-rows $cs-rows] n=[$count $cs-rows]]]
#]]
  [out-text [#
[leg1 eq=true n=2]
#]]
 ]

